    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341-a1">

                <pb facs="0599" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg537"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 657.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Professor Dunbar to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Topeka, Kansas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 2,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Would it be possible for you to
                    ascertain from the State Department of the Mexican Government whether that
                    government has ever had a treaty or official relations of any kind with the
                    Pawnee Indians who formerly occupied this State and Nebraska? The Pawnees claim
                    to have had some transactions with Mexico in the early part of this century and
                    perhaps earlier. I am preparing a vocabulary and grammar of their language for
                    publication by the government, and wish also to prepare a short historical
                    sketch of them to accompany it.</p>
                <p>If you could furnish me with any reliable data in the way indicated you will
                    confer a great favor.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN B. DUNBAR,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Professor of Greek,
                            Washburn College.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
